<div class="<%= layout_framework_classes %>">
  <div class="<%= layout_framework_title_classes %>">
    <%= render 'framework/page_header', page_name: :map %>
  </div>

  <div class="<%= layout_framework_content_classes %>">
    <%= render_framework_intro_paragraph(:map) %>

    <div class="space-y-16">
      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Usage') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            Maps are <%= link_to 'MapLibre GL JS', 'https://maplibre.org', target: :_blank, class: 'underline' %>
            compositions over <%= link_to 'OpenStreetMap', 'https://www.openstreetmap.org', target: :_blank, class: 'underline' %>
            vector tiles, and every layer is painted by the framework. The plugin runtime bundles a
            <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">TRMNLMaps</code> helper that builds the map style from
            the live screen, the way <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">TRMNLCharts</code> builds
            Highcharts options. The methods below are the ones these examples use;
            <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :paint_maps) %> carries the full list and the resolvers behind it.
          </p>

          <ul class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">options({ el, preset, center, zoom })</code>: the
              Map options for a still map, with the style for a preset, the container, and every handler and
              animation off.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">watch(el, buildFn)</code>: builds the map now and
              again when device, scale, mode, dark mode or theme changes, removing the previous one first.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">route(map, coords, { el, width })</code> and
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">dot(map, lngLat, { el, radius, hollow })</code>: plot a
              route and its markers as crisp fills painted from the screen's chart-series ramp.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">fit(map, coords, { padding, maxZoom })</code>: frames
              the coordinates on an integer zoom, with no animation.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">decodePolyline(str)</code>: a Google encoded polyline
              (the shape Strava returns) as <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">[lng, lat]</code> pairs.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">merge(base, overrides)</code>: layer your own layer ids,
              sources and Map options over the defaults.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">{ el }</code> is the map container id or element. Omit
            it on a single-screen plugin.
          </p>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            Four style presets ship: <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">streets</code> draws roads,
            water, parks, buildings and labels, <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">minimal</code> keeps
            the land, water and main roads a route sits on, <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">outline</code>
            is coast, water, main roads and the big place names for a small view, and
            <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">blank</code> is the land alone for your own overlays.
            Each preset is the same slot set drawn differently, so a theme restyles all four at once.
          </p>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">TRMNLMaps</code> resolves no paint of its own: every color
            comes from a <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">TRMNLPaint</code> map slot, so a map on a 1-bit
            screen draws dither tiles and a map on a color panel draws solids. For anything beyond MapLibre, read the
            slots directly: see <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :paint_api) %>.
          </p>

          <%= framework_heading(4, 'Tiles and keys') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            A map that names no tile source fetches TRMNL's own tiles (<code>maps.trmnl.com</code>) itself, and
            whoever renders the plugin pays nothing. Name a source when you have one:
          </p>
          <ul class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">options({ tiles: { url, key } })</code>: your own
              source. <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">url</code> is a
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">{z}/{x}/{y}</code> template and may carry
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">{key}</code>, which the key fills.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">options({ tiles: 'trmnl' })</code>: TRMNL's own source,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">maps.trmnl.com</code>, a Shortbread planet behind a CDN.
              The docs site and TRMNL's plugins use it.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">window.__TRMNL_MAPS__ = { tiles: { url, key } }</code>:
              set by the host per plugin instance, so a plugin author's key or a user's key from the plugin settings
              reaches the map without a key in the markup. A source named in code wins over it.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            The style speaks the Shortbread tile schema, so a source has to as well. Keep the OpenStreetMap credit
            whatever the source: the data is theirs either way.
          </p>

          <div class="<%= message_warning_classes %>">
            <div class="flex items-center w-full">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 items-center">
                <%= render 'shared/icons/warning' %>
              </div>
              <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-between ml-3">
                <p class="leading-none text-sm font-medium">
                  Maps are built non-interactive. A device has no input and the screenshot service captures one still
                  frame, so options() disables every handler and animation: set the camera in the options or with fit(),
                  never with flyTo or easeTo.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="<%= message_warning_classes %>">
            <div class="flex items-center w-full">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 items-center">
                <%= render 'shared/icons/warning' %>
              </div>
              <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-between ml-3">
                <p class="leading-none text-sm font-medium">
                  OpenStreetMap data is licensed under the ODbL and needs visible credit. watch() and attach() place a
                  framework-styled "&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors" label on every map: keep it.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="<%= message_sage_classes %>">
            <div class="flex items-center w-full">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 items-center">
                <%= render 'shared/icons/info' %>
              </div>
              <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-between ml-3">
                <p class="text-sm font-medium">
                  A plugin loads MapLibre GL JS from trmnl.com/js/maplibre-gl/5.24.0/, the same build the framework
                  serves next to the runtime for these examples, and the tiles come from maps.trmnl.com, so a map
                  renders an empty canvas without network. MapLibre is BSD licensed; the map data is
                  &copy; OpenStreetMap contributors.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <%= framework_heading(4, 'Streets') %>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              The streets preset on its own: one place, one zoom, nothing plotted. Load MapLibre from the framework,
              give the map a container with the map class, and build it inside watch().
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <script data-trmnl-src="/framework-docs/maplibre-gl-5.24.0.js"></script>
                  <link data-trmnl-href="/framework-docs/maplibre-gl-5.24.0.css" rel="stylesheet">

                  <div class="view view--full">
                    <div class="layout layout--col gap--small">
                      <div class="grid grid--cols-3">
                        <div class="item">
                          <div class="meta"></div>
                          <div class="content">
                            <span class="value value--small value--tnums">14&deg;C</span>
                            <span class="label">South Bank</span>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="item">
                          <div class="meta"></div>
                          <div class="content">
                            <span class="value value--small value--tnums">17:53</span>
                            <span class="label">Sunset</span>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="item">
                          <div class="meta"></div>
                          <div class="content">
                            <span class="value value--small value--tnums">2.1 km</span>
                            <span class="label">To the office</span>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>

                      <div id="map-streets" class="map stretch w--full"></div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="title_bar">
                      <img class="image image--adaptive" src="/images/plugins/trmnl--render.svg" alt="TRMNL Logo">
                      <span class="title">Map</span>
                      <span class="instance">Streets</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <script type="text/trmnl-example">
                    // Wait for both MapLibre and the framework's TRMNLMaps helper
                    // (bundled in the plugin runtime) before building the map.
                    function whenReady(cb) {
                      var tries = 0;
                      (function attempt() {
                        if (window.TRMNLMaps && window.maplibregl) return cb();
                        if (++tries > 200) return;
                        setTimeout(attempt, 50);
                      })();
                    }

                    whenReady(function () {
                      var el = "map-streets";
                      // watch() rebuilds on device/scale/mode/dark/theme change; options() carries
                      // the style for the preset, painted from the live screen.
                      TRMNLMaps.watch(el, function () {
                        return new maplibregl.Map(TRMNLMaps.options({
                          el: el, preset: "streets", center: [-0.1276, 51.5072], zoom: 13
                        }));
                      });
                    });
                  </script>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(demo_code: '<!-- import MapLibre GL JS and its stylesheet -->
<script src="https://trmnl.com/js/maplibre-gl/5.24.0/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
<link href="https://trmnl.com/js/maplibre-gl/5.24.0/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet">

<!-- markup with an empty, ID\'d .map container for the canvas -->
<div class="view view--full">
  <div class="layout layout--col gap--small">
    <div class="grid grid--cols-3">
      <div class="item">
        <div class="meta"></div>
        <div class="content">
          <span class="value value--small value--tnums">14&deg;C</span>
          <span class="label">South Bank</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <div class="meta"></div>
        <div class="content">
          <span class="value value--small value--tnums">17:53</span>
          <span class="label">Sunset</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <div class="meta"></div>
        <div class="content">
          <span class="value value--small value--tnums">2.1 km</span>
          <span class="label">To the office</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="map-streets" class="map stretch w--full"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="title_bar">
    <img class="image image--adaptive" src="/images/plugins/trmnl--render.svg" alt="TRMNL Logo">
    <span class="title">Map</span>
    <span class="instance">Streets</span>
  </div>
</div>

<script type="text/javascript">
  // Wait for MapLibre and the framework TRMNLMaps helper (bundled in the
  // plugin runtime), then build the map from the live screen.
  function whenReady(cb) {
    var tries = 0;
    (function attempt() {
      if (window.TRMNLMaps && window.maplibregl) return cb();
      if (++tries > 200) return;
      setTimeout(attempt, 50);
    })();
  }

  whenReady(function () {
    var el = "map-streets";
    // watch() rebuilds on device/scale/mode/dark/theme change; options() carries
    // the style for the preset, painted from the live screen.
    TRMNLMaps.watch(el, function () {
      return new maplibregl.Map(TRMNLMaps.options({
        el: el, preset: "streets", center: [-0.1276, 51.5072], zoom: 13
      }));
    });
  });
</script>') %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <%= framework_heading(4, 'Map styles') %>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              The same view through three presets. Streets is the full map, minimal keeps the shapes a route sits
              on, and outline is coast, water, main roads and the big names for the smallest views.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <script data-trmnl-src="/framework-docs/maplibre-gl-5.24.0.js"></script>
                  <link data-trmnl-href="/framework-docs/maplibre-gl-5.24.0.css" rel="stylesheet">

                  <div class="view view--full">
                    <div class="layout layout--col gap--small">
                      <div class="columns stretch">
                        <div class="column stretch">
                          <div class="layout layout--col gap--xsmall stretch">
                            <div id="map-style-streets" class="map stretch w--full"></div>
                            <span class="label label--small">streets</span>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="column stretch">
                          <div class="layout layout--col gap--xsmall stretch">
                            <div id="map-style-minimal" class="map stretch w--full"></div>
                            <span class="label label--small">minimal</span>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="column stretch">
                          <div class="layout layout--col gap--xsmall stretch">
                            <div id="map-style-outline" class="map stretch w--full"></div>
                            <span class="label label--small">outline</span>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="title_bar">
                      <img class="image image--adaptive" src="/images/plugins/trmnl--render.svg" alt="TRMNL Logo">
                      <span class="title">Map</span>
                      <span class="instance">Styles</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <script type="text/trmnl-example">
                    function whenReady(cb) {
                      var tries = 0;
                      (function attempt() {
                        if (window.TRMNLMaps && window.maplibregl) return cb();
                        if (++tries > 200) return;
                        setTimeout(attempt, 50);
                      })();
                    }

                    whenReady(function () {
                      ["streets", "minimal", "outline"].forEach(function (preset) {
                        var el = "map-style-" + preset;
                        TRMNLMaps.watch(el, function () {
                          return new maplibregl.Map(TRMNLMaps.options({
                            el: el, preset: preset, center: [2.3522, 48.8566], zoom: 12
                          }));
                        });
                      });
                    });
                  </script>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(demo_code: '// One watch() per container; only the preset changes.
["streets", "minimal", "outline"].forEach(function (preset) {
  var el = "map-style-" + preset;
  TRMNLMaps.watch(el, function () {
    return new maplibregl.Map(TRMNLMaps.options({
      el: el, preset: preset, center: [2.3522, 48.8566], zoom: 12
    }));
  });
});', language: 'javascript') %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <%= framework_heading(4, 'Markers and routes') %>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              Plot your own data. route() and dot() draw it as crisp fills painted from the screen's chart-series
              ramp, and fit() frames it on an integer zoom. A second route takes the next step of the ramp (a dither
              on 1-bit), so the ride in and the ride home read apart.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <script data-trmnl-src="/framework-docs/maplibre-gl-5.24.0.js"></script>
                  <link data-trmnl-href="/framework-docs/maplibre-gl-5.24.0.css" rel="stylesheet">

                  <div class="view view--full">
                    <div class="layout layout--col gap--small">
                      <div class="grid grid--cols-3">
                        <div class="item">
                          <div class="meta"></div>
                          <div class="content">
                            <span class="value value--small value--tnums">6.8 km</span>
                            <span class="label">Distance</span>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="item">
                          <div class="meta"></div>
                          <div class="content">
                            <span class="value value--small value--tnums">24 min</span>
                            <span class="label">Ride</span>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="item">
                          <div class="meta"></div>
                          <div class="content">
                            <span class="value value--small value--tnums">+41 m</span>
                            <span class="label">Climb</span>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>

                      <div id="map-commute" class="map stretch w--full"></div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="title_bar">
                      <img class="image image--adaptive" src="/images/plugins/trmnl--render.svg" alt="TRMNL Logo">
                      <span class="title">Map</span>
                      <span class="instance">Commute</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <script type="text/trmnl-example">
                    var route = [
                      [13.4240, 52.5390], [13.4205, 52.5352], [13.4150, 52.5310], [13.4088, 52.5265],
                      [13.4010, 52.5210], [13.3930, 52.5170], [13.3840, 52.5125], [13.3759, 52.5096]
                    ];
                    var home = [
                      [13.3759, 52.5096], [13.3850, 52.5150], [13.3960, 52.5232], [13.4060, 52.5290],
                      [13.4150, 52.5345], [13.4240, 52.5390]
                    ];

                    function whenReady(cb) {
                      var tries = 0;
                      (function attempt() {
                        if (window.TRMNLMaps && window.maplibregl) return cb();
                        if (++tries > 200) return;
                        setTimeout(attempt, 50);
                      })();
                    }

                    whenReady(function () {
                      var el = "map-commute";
                      TRMNLMaps.watch(el, function () {
                        var map = new maplibregl.Map(TRMNLMaps.options({ el: el, preset: "minimal" }));
                        map.on("load", function () {
                          // route() and dot() draw crisp fills from the chart-series ramp:
                          // the ride in takes step 0 of 2, the ride home step 1.
                          TRMNLMaps.route(map, route, { el: el, width: 3, i: 0, n: 2 });
                          TRMNLMaps.route(map, home, { el: el, id: "home", width: 3, i: 1, n: 2 });
                          TRMNLMaps.dot(map, route[0], { el: el, id: "start", radius: 5 });
                          TRMNLMaps.dot(map, route[route.length - 1], { el: el, id: "end", radius: 5, hollow: true });
                        });
                        // fit() frames both routes on an integer zoom, no animation.
                        TRMNLMaps.fit(map, route.concat(home), { padding: TRMNLPaint.px(24, { el: el }), maxZoom: 14 });
                        return map;
                      });
                    });
                  </script>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(demo_code: 'var route = [
  [13.4240, 52.5390], [13.4205, 52.5352], [13.4150, 52.5310], [13.4088, 52.5265],
  [13.4010, 52.5210], [13.3930, 52.5170], [13.3840, 52.5125], [13.3759, 52.5096]
];
var home = [
  [13.3759, 52.5096], [13.3850, 52.5150], [13.3960, 52.5232], [13.4060, 52.5290],
  [13.4150, 52.5345], [13.4240, 52.5390]
];

whenReady(function () {
  var el = "map-commute";
  TRMNLMaps.watch(el, function () {
    var map = new maplibregl.Map(TRMNLMaps.options({ el: el, preset: "minimal" }));
    map.on("load", function () {
      // route() and dot() draw crisp fills from the chart-series ramp:
      // the ride in takes step 0 of 2, the ride home step 1.
      TRMNLMaps.route(map, route, { el: el, width: 3, i: 0, n: 2 });
      TRMNLMaps.route(map, home, { el: el, id: "home", width: 3, i: 1, n: 2 });
      TRMNLMaps.dot(map, route[0], { el: el, id: "start", radius: 5 });
      TRMNLMaps.dot(map, route[route.length - 1], { el: el, id: "end", radius: 5, hollow: true });
    });
    // fit() frames both routes on an integer zoom, no animation.
    TRMNLMaps.fit(map, route.concat(home), { padding: TRMNLPaint.px(24, { el: el }), maxZoom: 14 });
    return map;
  });
});', language: 'javascript') %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <%= framework_heading(4, 'Grayscale and color') %>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              The map slots default to grays tuned for 1-bit: land and the built-up blocks are the canvas, water,
              parks and buildings are dither tiles, roads are grays short of the ink, labels are the ink. A full-color
              screen re-points the same slots at chromatic tokens and a limited palette dithers them to its ink set,
              so the plugin changes nothing.
            </p>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              Labels are framework elements placed over the canvas, so they take the screen's own fonts (TRMNL
              pixel fonts on 1-bit and 2-bit low-density panels, Inter on 4-bit and high density) with a large
              text stroke, on whole pixels. The biggest names win the space: small places wait for closer zooms,
              and a small map holds a few names instead of a crowd.
            </p>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              Switch the device picker to a color device or dark mode and the map repaints. A theme restyles the map
              with the same slot mixins it uses for every other component: see <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :theme_slots) %>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <script data-trmnl-src="/framework-docs/maplibre-gl-5.24.0.js"></script>
                  <link data-trmnl-href="/framework-docs/maplibre-gl-5.24.0.css" rel="stylesheet">

                  <div class="view view--full">
                    <div class="layout layout--col gap--small">
                      <div id="map-color" class="map stretch w--full"></div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="title_bar">
                      <img class="image image--adaptive" src="/images/plugins/trmnl--render.svg" alt="TRMNL Logo">
                      <span class="title">Map</span>
                      <span class="instance">Sydney Harbour</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <script type="text/trmnl-example">
                    function whenReady(cb) {
                      var tries = 0;
                      (function attempt() {
                        if (window.TRMNLMaps && window.maplibregl) return cb();
                        if (++tries > 200) return;
                        setTimeout(attempt, 50);
                      })();
                    }

                    whenReady(function () {
                      var el = "map-color";
                      TRMNLMaps.watch(el, function () {
                        return new maplibregl.Map(TRMNLMaps.options({
                          el: el, preset: "streets", center: [151.2153, -33.8568], zoom: 12
                        }));
                      });
                    });
                  </script>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(demo_code: '// Nothing here names a device or a color: the slots resolve per screen.
TRMNLMaps.watch(el, function () {
  return new maplibregl.Map(TRMNLMaps.options({
    el: el, preset: "streets", center: [151.2153, -33.8568], zoom: 12
