              positions its children already, so
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">top--3 left--3</code> measures from the map's own
              corner. Give the card a size and clamp its text, since nothing measures an element that is out of flow.
              <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :position) %> has the offset and stacking classes.
            </p>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              The bottom right corner belongs to the data credit, which has to stay visible. Place names land wherever
              the map data puts them, so a smaller card leaves more of them legible.
            </p>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              Over a detailed map, <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">outline--muted</code>
              <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :outline) %> draws that edge in a mid gray. It still separates the card from the
              map, with a quieter line across whatever it covers.
            </p>
